<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  StochCraft's vendor extensions to BPSim 2.0 and 1.0 (MIT OR Apache-2.0).

  BPSim's VendorExtension takes a `name` and, for its value, attributes and elements from another
  namespace, which a validator checks strictly: this schema declares StochCraft's. Validate with
  it imported next to the BPSim schema.

    <bpsim:VendorExtension name="stochcraft:queueCapacity"
        xmlns:stochcraft="https://helenkwok.github.io/StochCraft/bpsim/1" stochcraft:value="3"/>

  stochcraft:queueCapacity, on a task's ElementParameters: the most entities that wait for the
  task's resource (not counting those in service), a whole number of at least 0.

  stochcraft:pool, on a resource's ElementParameters, with the value true: the resource is a
  shared pool, even when one task uses it or none. Without it, a resource that one task needs a
  single unit of may be read as that task's own resource, unless its quantity has values
  validFor a calendar. With the value false, such a resource is that task's own even then: the
  task's units follow its shifts.

  stochcraft:batchSize, on a task's ElementParameters: the task collects this many entities
  (a whole number of at least 1) and sends them on together as one batch.

  stochcraft:unbatch, on a task's ElementParameters, with the value true: the task splits each
  batch back into its entities.

  stochcraft:quantity, on the ElementParameters of a sequence flow into a parallel gateway: how
  many entities from that flow go into each one the gateway sends on (a bill of materials;
  a whole number of at least 1).

  stochcraft:breakdown, on a task's ElementParameters: its resource's units fail after a time
  drawn from timeToFailure (elapsed since the last repair) and are repaired for a time drawn from
  repairTime, each holding one BPSim distribution or constant. Whether a failure interrupts the
  job under way is BPSim's own PriorityParameters/Interruptible. With handsOnWhileDown="false", a
  unit that fails while holding a finished part keeps it until repaired (by default it hands it
  on as soon as there is room).

    <bpsim:VendorExtension name="stochcraft:breakdown" xmlns:stochcraft="…">
      <stochcraft:breakdown>
        <stochcraft:timeToFailure><bpsim:ExponentialDistribution mean="480"/></stochcraft:timeToFailure>
        <stochcraft:repairTime><bpsim:TriangularDistribution min="10" mode="20" max="60"/></stochcraft:repairTime>
      </stochcraft:breakdown>
    </bpsim:VendorExtension>

  stochcraft:transferTime, on a task's ElementParameters: the time a part takes to reach the
  task from the element that sends it, holding one BPSim distribution or constant. The part
  takes its place in the task's buffer (queueCapacity) when the transfer starts and joins the
  queue when it ends; a sending task's resource stays occupied through the transfer, unless the
  attribute holdsSender is false: then it is free at once, and the time is a minimum time in the
  buffer.

    <bpsim:VendorExtension name="stochcraft:transferTime" xmlns:stochcraft="…">
      <stochcraft:transferTime holdsSender="false"><bpsim:FloatingParameter value="32"/></stochcraft:transferTime>
    </bpsim:VendorExtension>

  stochcraft:rework, on a sequence flow's ElementParameters, with the value true: entities
  taking it failed their quality requirements and go back to be worked on again (ISO 22400-2's
  rework quantity), counted against the last task with a resource of its own they finished at.

  stochcraft:patience, on a task's ElementParameters: the time an entity waits at the task before
  it gives up (reneging), drawn for each entity as it enters (before any transfer), holding one
  BPSim distribution or constant. With the attribute until="start" (the default) it gives up if
  no unit of the task's resource has taken it by then; with until="done", also if its service is
  not done by then (the unit finishes the job anyway, and the work is wasted). An entity that
  gives up takes the way out marked stochcraft:abandoned, or leaves the model. BPSim 2.0 has no
  parameter for this: its queueTime and waitTime are times every entity spends (they make up its
  lagTime), and a boundary timer's interTriggerTimer is a repeating interval, not a deadline
  drawn for each entity.

    <bpsim:VendorExtension name="stochcraft:patience" xmlns:stochcraft="…">
      <stochcraft:patience until="done"><bpsim:FloatingParameter value="30"/></stochcraft:patience>
    </bpsim:VendorExtension>

  stochcraft:healthCheck, on a task's ElementParameters: each unit of the task's resource is
  checked every interval (its own checks, the first one interval after the start) and fails a
  check when more entities wait at the task than limit per unit working (not failed, not out and
  on shift); a unit that fails is out of service for the restart time, then comes back. The
  optional keep is the fewest units left working: a failed check takes no unit out below it.
  onTakeout="retry" (the default) sends a job under way on a unit taken out back to the head of
  the queue at once (its work is wasted); onTakeout="resume" lets it wait on the unit and resume
  after the restart. With a finite waiting room, an entity keeps its place throughout (back in
  the queue, or waiting on its unit); placeWhileOut="reserved" (the default) has a unit taken out
  keep a place for itself while it restarts, as a failed unit does: once the job under way (if
  any) is back in the queue, it takes a place that is free at that moment, if one is, and gives
  it back when its restart ends, so the buffer holds fewer while units are out.
  placeWhileOut="open" has it hold none, as a unit off shift. With an unlimited waiting room it
  changes nothing. BPSim 2.0 has nothing for it.

    <bpsim:VendorExtension name="stochcraft:healthCheck" xmlns:stochcraft="…">
      <stochcraft:healthCheck limit="2" keep="3">
        <stochcraft:interval><bpsim:FloatingParameter value="10"/></stochcraft:interval>
        <stochcraft:restart><bpsim:FloatingParameter value="60"/></stochcraft:restart>
      </stochcraft:healthCheck>
    </bpsim:VendorExtension>

  stochcraft:onShiftEnd, on a task's ElementParameters, with the value finish, retry or resume:
  what happens to a job under way on a unit of the task's own resource that goes off shift (the
  units on shift drop, by the resource's quantity validFor a calendar, or its availability
  ends). finish (the default) lets the unit finish the job, then go off; retry sends it back to
  the head of the queue at once (its work is wasted); resume lets it wait on the unit and carry
  on with what was left when the unit is on shift again. Units go off idle ones first, then
  failed or restarting ones, then busy ones, the job started last first.

    <bpsim:VendorExtension name="stochcraft:onShiftEnd"
        xmlns:stochcraft="https://helenkwok.github.io/StochCraft/bpsim/1" stochcraft:value="retry"/>

  stochcraft:abandoned, on a sequence flow's ElementParameters, with the value true: the way out
  of a task with a patience that entities giving up take (a retry, a call back later), besides
  the task's ordinary way out.

  stochcraft:scrap, on an end event's ElementParameters: what reaches it is scrap (ISO
  22400-2's scrap quantity), counted against the task the attribute chargedTo names (an
  inspection rejecting work done upstream), or else the last task with a resource of its own
  each entity finished at.

    <bpsim:VendorExtension name="stochcraft:scrap" xmlns:stochcraft="…">
      <stochcraft:scrap chargedTo="machine"/>
    </bpsim:VendorExtension>

  stochcraft:demand, on an end event's ElementParameters: the customer demand it serves, for
  takt (the available time divided by the demand over it): quantity parts per run (the measured
  window), day, week or shift. With calendar, only the time that calendar is active counts as
  available, and with per="shift" each active period of it is a shift (needed then).

    <bpsim:VendorExtension name="stochcraft:demand" xmlns:stochcraft="…">
      <stochcraft:demand quantity="480" per="shift" calendar="day-shift"/>
    </bpsim:VendorExtension>

  stochcraft:plannedRunTime, on a task's ElementParameters: the planned time for the task's
  resource to make one item (ISO 22400-2's planned runtime per item), holding one BPSim
  distribution or constant whose mean is the plan. It is not simulated; results use it for
  effectiveness and OEE.

    <bpsim:VendorExtension name="stochcraft:plannedRunTime" xmlns:stochcraft="…">
      <stochcraft:plannedRunTime><bpsim:FloatingParameter value="30"/></stochcraft:plannedRunTime>
    </bpsim:VendorExtension>

  stochcraft:changeover, on a task's ElementParameters: its resource's unit sets up before a part
  only when the part's value of the token property named by the attribute property differs from
  that of the part the unit served last (its first part needs none). The setup takes the time of
  the stochcraft:change whose from and to are the two values, else stochcraft:time, each holding
  one BPSim distribution or constant. A setup before every job is BPSim's own
  TimeParameters/SetUpTime.

    <bpsim:VendorExtension name="stochcraft:changeover" xmlns:stochcraft="…">
      <stochcraft:changeover property="type">
        <stochcraft:time><bpsim:FloatingParameter value="10"/></stochcraft:time>
        <stochcraft:change from="A" to="B"><bpsim:FloatingParameter value="25"/></stochcraft:change>
      </stochcraft:changeover>
    </bpsim:VendorExtension>

  stochcraft:processingTimeBy, on a task's ElementParameters: processing times by the value of
  the token property named by the attribute property (a time by product type). A token whose
  value, as text, is the value of a stochcraft:time takes that time, a BPSim distribution or
  constant; any other token (another value, or none) takes the task's own
  TimeParameters/ProcessingTime. Each value appears once.

    <bpsim:VendorExtension name="stochcraft:processingTimeBy" xmlns:stochcraft="…">
      <stochcraft:processingTimeBy property="type">
        <stochcraft:time value="A"><bpsim:FloatingParameter value="6"/></stochcraft:time>
        <stochcraft:time value="B"><bpsim:FloatingParameter value="20"/></stochcraft:time>
      </stochcraft:processingTimeBy>
    </bpsim:VendorExtension>

  stochcraft:routing, on an exclusive gateway's ElementParameters, with the value shortestQueue
  (or standard, BPMN's own routing): each entity goes to the way with the fewest entities waiting
  or in transit among those with room, a tie to the way taken longest ago; while no way has
  room, the element sending into the gateway waits (a task's resource stays blocked) and a
  start event's arrival is lost.

  stochcraft:power, on a task's ElementParameters: the power each unit of the task's resource
  draws in each state, in kilowatts (numbers of at least 0): processing and idle (both needed),
  and blocked, failed and offShift, each idle when left out.

    <bpsim:VendorExtension name="stochcraft:power" xmlns:stochcraft="…">
      <stochcraft:power processing="12.5" idle="2" failed="0.5" offShift="0"/>
    </bpsim:VendorExtension>

  stochcraft:stopCount, on an element's ElementParameters: each replication ends once this many
  entities (a whole number of at least 1) have left the element since time 0 (for an end event:
  arrived there), or at the scenario's duration if that comes first.

  stochcraft:stopWhenEmpty, on a task's ElementParameters, with the value true: each replication
  ends the first time the task holds no entity, none waiting and none in service, after it has
  taken one in.

  stochcraft:estimate, on the ElementParameters of an element with a time distribution (a start
  event's interTriggerTimer, a task's processingTime): the three-point estimate the distribution
  was fitted from, kept as its pedigree. The distribution itself is the standard BPSim one in the
  parameters; this records where it came from. Exactly one of max and p95.

    <bpsim:VendorExtension name="stochcraft:estimate" xmlns:stochcraft="…">
      <stochcraft:estimate family="pert" min="10" mode="20" max="60" source="Delphi, round 2"/>
    </bpsim:VendorExtension>
-->
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
    xmlns:stochcraft="https://helenkwok.github.io/StochCraft/bpsim/1"
    targetNamespace="https://helenkwok.github.io/StochCraft/bpsim/1"
    elementFormDefault="qualified">
  <xs:attribute name="value" type="xs:string"/>
  <xs:complexType name="Value">
    <xs:sequence>
      <xs:any namespace="http://www.bpsim.org/schemas/2.0 http://www.bpsim.org/schemas/1.0"
          processContents="lax"/>
    </xs:sequence>
  </xs:complexType>
  <xs:element name="breakdown">
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:sequence>
        <xs:element name="timeToFailure" type="stochcraft:Value"/>
        <xs:element name="repairTime" type="stochcraft:Value"/>
      </xs:sequence>
      <xs:attribute name="handsOnWhileDown" type="xs:boolean" default="true"/>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="transferTime">
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:complexContent>
        <xs:extension base="stochcraft:Value">
          <xs:attribute name="holdsSender" type="xs:boolean" default="true"/>
        </xs:extension>
      </xs:complexContent>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="plannedRunTime" type="stochcraft:Value"/>
  <xs:element name="patience">
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:complexContent>
        <xs:extension base="stochcraft:Value">
          <xs:attribute name="until" default="start">
            <xs:simpleType>
              <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
                <xs:enumeration value="start"/>
                <xs:enumeration value="done"/>
              </xs:restriction>
            </xs:simpleType>
          </xs:attribute>
        </xs:extension>
      </xs:complexContent>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="healthCheck">
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:sequence>
        <xs:element name="interval" type="stochcraft:Value"/>
        <xs:element name="restart" type="stochcraft:Value"/>
      </xs:sequence>
      <xs:attribute name="limit" use="required">
        <xs:simpleType>
          <xs:restriction base="xs:double">
            <xs:minInclusive value="0"/>
          </xs:restriction>
        </xs:simpleType>
      </xs:attribute>
      <xs:attribute name="keep" type="xs:nonNegativeInteger"/>
      <xs:attribute name="onTakeout" default="retry">
        <xs:simpleType>
          <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
            <xs:enumeration value="retry"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="resume"/>
          </xs:restriction>
        </xs:simpleType>
      </xs:attribute>
      <xs:attribute name="placeWhileOut" default="reserved">
        <xs:simpleType>
          <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
            <xs:enumeration value="reserved"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="open"/>
          </xs:restriction>
        </xs:simpleType>
      </xs:attribute>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="demand">
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:attribute name="quantity" type="xs:double" use="required"/>
      <xs:attribute name="per" use="required">
        <xs:simpleType>
          <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
            <xs:enumeration value="run"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="day"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="week"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="shift"/>
          </xs:restriction>
        </xs:simpleType>
      </xs:attribute>
      <xs:attribute name="calendar" type="xs:string"/>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="scrap">
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:attribute name="chargedTo" type="xs:string"/>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="changeover">
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:sequence>
        <xs:element name="time" type="stochcraft:Value"/>
        <xs:element name="change" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
          <xs:complexType>
            <xs:complexContent>
              <xs:extension base="stochcraft:Value">
                <xs:attribute name="from" type="xs:string" use="required"/>
                <xs:attribute name="to" type="xs:string" use="required"/>
              </xs:extension>
            </xs:complexContent>
          </xs:complexType>
        </xs:element>
      </xs:sequence>
      <xs:attribute name="property" type="xs:string" use="required"/>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="processingTimeBy">
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:sequence>
        <xs:element name="time" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
          <xs:complexType>
            <xs:complexContent>
              <xs:extension base="stochcraft:Value">
                <xs:attribute name="value" type="xs:string" use="required"/>
              </xs:extension>
            </xs:complexContent>
          </xs:complexType>
        </xs:element>
      </xs:sequence>
      <xs:attribute name="property" type="xs:string" use="required"/>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="power">
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:attribute name="processing" type="xs:double" use="required"/>
      <xs:attribute name="idle" type="xs:double" use="required"/>
      <xs:attribute name="blocked" type="xs:double"/>
      <xs:attribute name="failed" type="xs:double"/>
      <xs:attribute name="offShift" type="xs:double"/>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="estimate">
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:attribute name="family" use="required">
        <xs:simpleType>
          <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
            <xs:enumeration value="triangular"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="pert"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="lognormal"/>
            <xs:enumeration value="weibull"/>
          </xs:restriction>
        </xs:simpleType>
      </xs:attribute>
      <xs:attribute name="min" type="xs:double" use="required"/>
      <xs:attribute name="mode" type="xs:double" use="required"/>
      <xs:attribute name="max" type="xs:double"/>
      <xs:attribute name="p95" type="xs:double"/>
      <xs:attribute name="source" type="xs:string"/>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
</xs:schema>
